ll House using the triplet of 7s and the lowest pair of 8s. This clears 5 cards at once and simplifies my remaining hand to two pairs, a single, and control cards. Playing the single Q first is less optimal because it is easily beaten by K or A, forcing me to use my top cards early. The Full House is a stronger opening that tests the opponents\' strength.\n\nReason: This move clears the most cards (5) while getting rid of the weakest pair (8s). It leaves a strong defensive hand with high pairs (JJ, KK) and top cards (2, Black Joker) to control the flow later.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠7", "♥7", "♦7", "♥8", "♣8"]}'}
